id: pm-3crymx
title: "A declared context intent returns no context when combined with the narrowing flag, and its refusal receipt reports 122 tokens against a 2400 budget as the reason it does not fit"
description: "Measured 2026-08-16 on this tracker. pm context --for orient returns context (7832 bytes, ~1958 tok, under its declared 2400 ceiling). pm context --for orient --limit 10 returns no context at all: budget_exceeded.omitted_result true, reason declared_budget_infeasible. Adding the narrowing flag destroys the answer. The emitted receipt then reports estimated_tokens 122 against token_budget 2400 with within_budget false and declaration_feasible false, because the final updateContextIntentEstimate call in applyContextIntentProjection re-estimates over the refusal object it just built, overwriting the estimate that justified the refusal. The number shown is not the number compared. Both named recoveries are also wrong: narrowing the request is what caused the omission, and --token-budget 20000 still omits. --token-budget 200000 succeeds and emits estimated_tokens 132522 under an intent whose declaration is 2400, because an explicit budget replaces the declared ceiling rather than being bounded by it."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:cli","area:context",context-management,receipts,token-budget
created_at: "2026-08-16T10:50:36.737Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T10:51:25.662Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "A refusal receipt reports the estimate that produced the refusal, never an estimate recomputed over the refusal itself, and a test asserts the reported estimated_tokens exceeds token_budget whenever result_omitted is true; Applying an explicit row bound to a declared intent never produces a smaller result set and a larger reported cost than the same intent without it; Recovery guidance for an infeasible declaration names a recovery that is verified to work on the corpus that produced the refusal, rather than a generic instruction; An explicit --token-budget above a declared intent ceiling either is refused, is clamped to the declaration, or emits an explicit receipt field stating that the declaration was overridden and by how much; A negative control proves each assertion fails when the defect is reintroduced"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: high
confidence: high
expected_result: "A declared intent bounds a read and reports honestly why, and narrowing the request never removes the answer."
actual_result: context --for orient --limit 10 omits the result entirely and justifies it with a number 20x under the bound it claims to have exceeded.
